{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread","id":1517651,"title":"(1e) Vampire: The Requiem Nostalgia Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-10T09:56:02-07:00","id":1517651,"title":"(1e) Vampire: The Requiem Nostalgia Thread","content":"So, I was lurking through the Gargoyles thread and a burst of nostalgia hit me. So I decided to make this thread as a spin-off of sorts. For context, here's my post from that thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles?p=1517630#post1517630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this counts as thread necromancy or comes off as too much of a tangent, but reading this thread reminded me of why I fell in love with Requiem 1e way back when I was young.<br /> <br /> There was an open-ended weirdness within the whole World of Darkness at the time, especially when all you had were just the two core rulebooks and your own imagination, which was how my friends and I played for years. Gargoyles were a surprisingly common encounter in our games. None of us knew much about the original WoD setting from the 90's aside from the fact it existed at one point and so we didn't have nostalgia goggles on when we played Requiem for the first time (not yet at least, lol). We didn't get the chance to buy Werewolf or Mage back then, so we just made our own rules for lupines and magi because they were mentioned briefly in the core rules. Our group eventually got Hunter and Changeling and a few supplements like Armory and Nomads a couple years later, but that was it.<br /> <br /> Requiem 1e's corebook had weird stuff like Gargoyles, Homunculi, and Hellhounds that were never really brought up again until way later if they even got brought up again at all. A lot of people just forgot about them completely and some of that stuff didn't carry over into 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For further context, I first started RPG's in late 2003 when I was ten years old with D&amp;D 3.5, or more accurately, a heavily house ruled homebrew variant of it. My Dad was my first GM and he grew up on the classic Advanced Dungeons &amp; Dragons from the 1980's, and was able to simplify the game for me, my stepbrothers, and my friends to understand easier and he also taught me to be a pretty good GM.<br /> <br /> By late 2004, we were all growing tired of medieval fantasy and wanted something darker, edgier, and with a far more modern setting. Keep in mind that me, my stepbrothers, and my two friends were the kind of kids who loved stuff like InuYasha, Kingdom Hearts, Underworld, Hellsing, and Devil May Cry unironically and a lot of us were also wannabe gun nuts too. I even tried to come up with rules for guns in D&amp;D. Not muskets or arquebuses either, but modern automatic firearms. We didn't know about d20 Modern at the time or anything like that, so we thought all RPG's were either medieval fantasy or sci-fi. We knew about Shadowrun and the Star Wars RPG but never actually got to play either of them, go figure.<br /> <br /> Around that same time, Dad tells me about Vampire: The Masquerade and White Wolf and the basic premise of the World of Darkness games. I instantly fall in love with the basic concept. Even moreso after playing the Hunter: The Reckoning PS2 game around that same time and finding out it's set in the same world as VTM. I also found out about Masquerade's then-recent end and the Requiem reboot.<br /> <br /> So naturally, I wanted to buy this game and check it out. I saved up enough of my allowance money and birthday money from earlier in the year that I was able to get both the World of Darkness corebook and the Requiem book at the B. Dalton bookstore in the mall during their after-Christmas sales. I instantly fell in love with the idea of a game set in a dark modern gothic world. There were a few things I didn't care for, but I'll get to that in a bit.<br /> <br /> I spent the first two weeks of that January obsessively reading the two books and memorizing the rules as best I could, taking notes and trying to come up with some setting and rules hacks to make the game more appealing to me and my group. I'd take the books to school and read them during recess, writing in my notebook as I came up with an idea for a campaign.<br /> <br /> Now, let's get the elephant in the room out of the way. Me and my friends never did personal horror. Back then, we always found that aspect kind of lame and boring. To us, it felt like they were trying to make the game seem more artsy than it was and as we came from D&amp;D 3.5 and were into stuff like anime, action movies, and vidya, we went full &quot;Supers with fangs&quot; as some of the fandom may derisively call it.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, we also eventually did a sort of troupe play with me, my best friend, and one of my brothers alternating as the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Our characters were cool, they dressed like Hot Topic mall goths (or Tetsuya Nomura character designs) and we all looked like anime characters (no joke, we'd print off anime and manga pics we found on Google Images for our characters if we couldn't draw them ourselves) and yeah, our PC's even carried katanas, keyblades (yes, really) and lots of guns. In my defense, I was eleven years old when I first started getting into WoD and was probably too young to be playing something like Requiem,<br /> <br /> The combat system wasn't the best for the kinds of games we ran, but we didn't know any better nor did we care. Lots of mortal criminals, Belial's Brood cultists, VII assassins, gargoyles, and hellhounds got their asses kicked by our characters. It was fun.<br /> <br /> We were aware the other WoD games existed but we never got to buy the corebooks for them nor did we ever get any supplements (we were tweens after all) but we did want to include werewolves and mages in our games to the point I even came up with a crude kitbashed system for mages. Rather than using something like Cruac or Theban Sorcery as a guideline, I actually tried to copy and paste spells from Dungeons &amp; Dragons into the game but arranged them in a five-dot range like Disciplines with the different schools of magic being treated almost like Disciplines. It was janky as fuck, but it worked well enough. Magic was treated as a homebrew four-dot merit that mortals could take and they got two dots worth of spells for it<br /> <br /> I can't remember what I did for werewolves, but I remember I tried to stat them up as an elite antagonist meant for boss battles (we all had seen Underworld and Van Helsing by that point, after all) but I don't think anyone ever played a werewolf. My youngest brother did play a mage with our homebrew rules after his Nosferatu got killed.<br /> <br /> We played on and off for over two years, from late January 2005 up until the spring of 2007. My brothers and I continued playing for about two more years but it was more sporadic. We did get to try Changeling The Lost though and it blew us away!<br /> <br /> I moved out of town in 2007 shortly after I turned fourteen and started high school. I drifted away from Requiem and RPG's in general but later got into Masquerade around the time V20 came out. I did get to play a few one shots Requiem 2e and it's a damn fine system that much better fits the personal horror themes intended by the game. With that said, I prefer Requiem 1e, or more accurately, the weird and heavily homebrewed variant of it I played as a middle schooler. Much like cocaine, nostalgia is a hell of a drug.<br /> <br /> On a more personal level, I think playing Requiem 1e helped me better explore my issues with gender identity as all my Vampire PC's were men. At one point, I even played a Daeva PC who was pretty much the yaoi bishonen equivalent of the infamous &quot;Lesbian Stripper Ninja&quot; meme. In my defense, I didn't know any better and the rest of my all-male group was surprisingly cool with it (so long as I didn't hit on their characters). But I'm not sure I'd ever have worked up the courage to transition and be my true self were it not for those gonzo Requiem chronicles all those years ago.<br /> <br /> Now don't get me wrong, nowadays I actually enjoy more serious dramatic personal horror games like the World of Darkness (or Chronicles as it's now called) was originally intended for. Requiem 2e is honestly one of the better games for that sort of play, especially with the systems of touchstones, banes, and Humanity being more tied to being like an actual human being instead of just a glorified morality meter like it was in 1e.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I'm not gonna lie and say that I don't miss those days of bishie vampires dressed to the nines in Hot Topic chic, wielding keyblades, fighting gargoyles and Brood cultists, and trying to score money and artifacts.<br /> <br /> But enough of my own nostalgia-fueled ramblings, tell me your favorite memories from Requiem's first edition!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 02-11-2024, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T14:53:05-07:00","id":1517829,"title":"","content":"Being honest, I didn't really played 1st edition myself, but was the first ttrpg book I have read. I was a teenager, I can't quite remember the year, but Requiem was fairly new. I was really into video games, and crossed paths with bloodlines, after playing it, I watched a video which told more about it, and told they come from ttrpg, which was something I had never heard about it at the time. After some research I read about Requiem was the successor of masquerade. So I got World of Darkness and Vampire the Requiem books. Well I fell in love with it. I liked vampires since Symphony of the night, but Requiem vampires captured exactly the image I had about it.<br /> <br /> Sorry any typo! My keyboard is kinda strange","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T16:20:46-07:00","id":1517838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1517829#post1517829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being honest, I didn't really played 1st edition myself, but was the first ttrpg book I have read. I was a teenager, I can't quite remember the year, but Requiem was fairly new. I was really into video games, and crossed paths with bloodlines, after playing it, I watched a video which told more about it, and told they come from ttrpg, which was something I had never heard about it at the time. After some research I read about Requiem was the successor of masquerade. So I got World of Darkness and Vampire the Requiem books. Well I fell in love with it. I liked vampires since Symphony of the night, but Requiem vampires captured exactly the image I had about it.<br /> <br /> Sorry any typo! My keyboard is kinda strange</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Kind of reminds me how I got into Requiem. I had heard of Masquerade and the old WoD setting through a mix of my Dad mentioning it to me, the Hunter: The Reckoning PS2 game, and a few magazine ads for Bloodlines which is why I decided to look it up on Google and Wikipedia, which led me to Requiem and I became hyped. Me, my two brothers, and my friend were big fans of Underworld, Hellsing, Van Helsing, BloodRayne, Symphony of the Night, and of course the more classic stuff like The Lost Boys, Fright Night, and Bram Stoker's Dracula.<br /> <br /> I got the nWoD and Requiem 1e corebooks as soon as I got the chance that New Year's Eve and I still sometimes get goosebumps thinking about all those nights reading the corebooks and immersing myself in the books and the World of Darkness as I came up with the ideas for our first chronicle","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T18:26:57-07:00","id":1517852,"title":"","content":"I gripe about 1E a lot because I've had to dig through so many half-baked mechanics and ideas for 2E updates, but even then, it's an immensely playable, accessible RPG. The setting is rich but easy to understand in the broad strokes, the character options are very straightforward and evocative, and it feels very polished and complete compared with its predecessor. As much as I love 2E, it's not quite as easy to pick up, and expects a bit more foreknowledge of the CofD setting. If you want a political game about scrappy, street-level vampires, First Edition Requiem is a great place to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 07-13-2023, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T22:04:03-07:00","id":1517860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1517852#post1517852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gripe about 1E a lot because I've had to dig through so many half-baked mechanics and ideas for 2E updates, but what even then, it's an immensely playable, accessible RPG. The setting is rich but easy to understand in the broad strokes, the character options are very straightforward and evocative, and it feels very polished and complete compared with its predecessor. As much as I love 2E, it's not quite as easy to pick up, and expects a bit more foreknowledge of the CofD setting. If you want a political game about scrappy, street-level vampires, First Edition Requiem is a great place to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on all of this. 2e is great for what it's supposed to be. It's a more polished and refined game aimed more for the personal horror chronicle style and more importantly, it was designed with the intent of fully divorcing Requiem from Masquerade instead of trying to replace it while incorporating several years worth of updates and changes and it shows. Requiem 2e was squarely aimed at those people who already knew about nWoD/CofD in some capacity and it was aiming for a very specific frame of mind and a very specific playstyle, even more than Requiem 1e did.<br /> <br /> I've played in a few Requiem 2e one-shots and enjoyed myself greatly, but I could never see myself ever trying to ST a 2e chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T04:31:11-07:00","id":1517865,"title":"","content":"Truth be told, i have yet to experiment with 2e to get a clearer idea of in what ways things have changed between editions, since i stick to my 1e materials pretty much out of habit (and having no Requiem group currently, truth be told).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T10:02:09-07:00","id":1517885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1517865#post1517865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, i have yet to experiment with 2e to get a clearer idea of in what ways things have changed between editions, since i stick to my 1e materials pretty much out of habit (and having no Requiem group currently, truth be told).</div> </div> </div> </div>1e has a lot of great material and as good as 2e is, I actually like 1e a lot more. <br /> <br /> Hell, I got a fuckton of mileage out of just the two 1e corebooks and my own imagination back in the day","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T12:58:59-07:00","id":1517893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread#post1517651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .Our characters were cool, they dressed like Hot Topic mall goths (or Tetsuya Nomura character designs) and we all looked like anime characters (no joke, we'd print off anime and manga pics we found on Google Images for our characters if we couldn't draw them ourselves) and yeah, our PC's even carried katanas, keyblades (yes, really) and lots of guns. In my defense, I was eleven years old when I first started getting into WoD and was probably too young to be playing something like Requiem,. . .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, we did that, like ten-years prior in '92 - '94 playing Cyperpunk 2020; we had are style, and goth-gear, etc. Just like supernatural, except with cybernetics. Then, we got into Masquerade in June of '94. I thought it was lame, playing vampires that is, until I actually played a session. I really started to like vampires after reading Ann Rice as stories about immortals, not gothy vamps. Though, half my friends were goths that played to be gothy-vamps and the other half were power-gamers that had to win and be stronger than others in the game. Yeah, OK. <br /> <br /> As tweens, we all played AD&amp;D and moved on to Battletech, and back and forth. <br /> <br /> 2004, I was working my first, real full-time job you get out of college, as that's what, you're <i>suppose</i> to do. I was not liking the sucking up of my free-time I could be using towards RPG-games. Back then, we were in to Dark Ages, and I actually had no idea Requiem or NWoD even existed until '05 or '06. <br /> <br /> I loved Requiem a lot more than Masquerade; Blood-potency, virtues and vices are awesome; it's as if every question every V:tM player ever asked was included in Requiem. <br /> <br /> As for Chronicles, well, I don't want to relearn a system I haven't fully understood, so I stick with NWoD, but, I do like some of CoD such as variable sunlight damage, etc. and the best part is, we also homebrew and we pick and choose the rules we play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T10:22:12-07:00","id":1518052,"title":"","content":"I appreciated the fact that VTR left the origins of vampires as vague as possible and giving us the freedom to come up with our own ideas and that given enough time that a Kindred could reach the general power level of a 3rd generation monster and how to create bloodlines for the 5 main clans as I did like the smaller number of clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-16-2023, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T14:04:52-07:00","id":1518081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1518052#post1518052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciated the fact that VTR left the origins of vampires as vague as possible and giving us the freedom to come up with our own ideas and that given enough time that a Kindred could reach the general power level of a 3rd generation and how to create bloodlines for the 5 main clans as I did like the smaller number of clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I liked the fact VTR had less clans but the clans were more broad. We never played any of the bloodlines in our old games and I only played a bloodline once in someone else's game many years later but Lord knows we made up several very broken homebrew Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Requiem presented five bloodlines and three of them were just remakes of VTM clans, but that was still good enough for providing a template for ST's to make their own bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T15:53:06-07:00","id":1518093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1517885#post1517885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1e has a lot of great material and as good as 2e is, I actually like 1e a lot more.<br /> <br /> Hell, I got a fuckton of mileage out of just the two 1e corebooks and my own imagination back in the day</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, i haven't delved into 2e nowhere near enough to say i prefer 1e with any fair reason beyond laziness to re-learning the basics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Not like V5 that i recently tried out and called quits due to how terribly disorganized and unhelpful the corebook can be if you don't read it start to finish, no matter that you have played VtM for decades and already knows 2/3 to 90% of the contents. Seriously, i'm too old to tolerate a book being this obnoxious to me, specially when my curiosity was only mild at best. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But can't deny 1e VtR has plenty to tinker and mess with, what is at least half the reason i never felt much of an urge to update/retool into 2e (even if the cutting down on bloodline disciplines could be nice). Some fun changes but nothing that screams &quot;i need this&quot; to me that some quick retool wouldn't cover. Guess i'm too &quot;ensonced to move&quot;\u200b when it comes to VtR editions.<br /> <br /> (Beside the fact i don't even have a Requiem group at present - my current chronicle is a V20 homebrew atrocity of houserules, some VtR inspired, some not, and cryptolore mix of editions and videogames of my own)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-15-2023, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T10:50:49-07:00","id":1518145,"title":"","content":"I normally didn\u2019t play any bloodlines in the setting as I felt the main clan was enough to serve my game playing needs , but I did have a liking for a couple of the Gangrel offshoots like the Boghande that could manipulate luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-16-2023, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T11:57:05-07:00","id":1518148,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it. I never tried to create a bloodline for any of the 5 clans as I was stuck on what facet they could fill that the parent clan didn\u2019t cover or the general Covenant for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T15:02:54-07:00","id":1518155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1518148#post1518148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it. I never tried to create a bloodline for any of the 5 clans as I was stuck on what facet they could fill that the parent clan didn\u2019t cover or the general Covenant for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously, the Bohagande that you previously cited are a very clear example of a bloodline whose niche is no way particularly thematic or resonant with their parent clan, beyond the contrivance of a shapechanging-based confusion tied in their origin backstory, that is.<br /> <br /> <br /> Me, the most i have messed with things lore/setting-wise was by making a &quot;lost&quot; clan in more than one of my chronicles, though just one per chronicle to be fair.<br /> <br /> Though that is also because i have more than once used canon &quot;lost clans&quot; like the Julii, Akhud, Xolotl, Grettir or whatever elusive things might be behind the origins of the Annunaki (from the Invictus book, that as written would be older than Ventrue AND Gangrel both, not to mention the Camarilla the Invictus claims to originate from), the Gorgons (Ventrue line from CotC) or the Vedma (OD, claim to predate the Gangrel), among others.<br /> <br /> Maybe one of those days i'll do a &quot;make 5 bloodlines for a homebrew clan&quot; challenge to myself just for fun and the world-building exercise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T21:03:28-07:00","id":1518164,"title":"","content":"(I write with Google Translate)<br /> VtR has been released in Japanese (1e), but it is very minor.<br /> <br /> My first VtR character was a ghoul.<br /> My first VtR play was on a Japanese irc channel, 1 storyteller, 1 player.<br /> <br /> I was trying hard to decipher &quot;TheBlood&quot; and &quot;Ghouls&quot; with Google Translate.<br /> It was a pity that clanbook was difficult to translate with Google due to the layout <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1e and 2e both have their good points and both have their bad points.<br /> I thought about 1.7e, which incorporates the good points, but VtR has multiple rules intertwined, so it's quite difficult.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25958-veiros","name":"veiros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25958_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T21:37:59-07:00","id":1518167,"title":"","content":"I always pondered the possibility of Requiem having an unofficial &quot;1.5&quot; edition/era that came before 2e but I'm not quite sure when, where, and how it emerged. It's kinda hard for me to properly describe the difference between early Requiem 1e and the later 1e material/Requiem 1.5. but you know it when you see it.<br /> <br /> I know for a fact that <i>Danse Macabre, Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</i>, and <i>Requiem for Rome </i>were definitely part of that unofficial &quot;1.5&quot; era, but I'm unsure if it begins with Requiem for Rome or before it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T22:00:27-07:00","id":1518168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1518167#post1518167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always pondered the possibility of Requiem having an unofficial &quot;1.5&quot; edition/era that came before 2e but I'm not quite sure when, where, and how it emerged. It's kinda hard for me to properly describe the difference between early Requiem 1e and the later 1e material/Requiem 1.5. but you know it when you see it.<br /> <br /> I know for a fact that <i>Danse Macabre, Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</i>, and <i>Requiem for Rome </i>were definitely part of that unofficial &quot;1.5&quot; era, but I'm unsure if it begins with Requiem for Rome or before it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, to my understanding Requiem for Rome and the clanbooks around the time Rose Bailey took over as the line developer, is about the point that Requiem hit what's generally considered version 1.5 in terms of its handling and approach \u2014 the start of that process alluded to in 2e whereby it was taking steps to distinguish itself as separate from Masquerade in a more definite sense than making statements with its ludonarrative toolkit meant to directly contrast with its classic World of Darkness predecessor.<br /> <br /> I couldn't tell you if it started sooner without checking the credits on all the books, but it had definitely at least started up by the time the Strix were being introduced as a phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T09:55:19-07:00","id":1518179,"title":"","content":"Playing a Gangrel gunslinger or Nosferatu clan lore master that looked completely normal was so much fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T14:19:18-07:00","id":1518204,"title":"","content":"Fire &amp; pointy wooden sticks - it's very curious indeed that two of the core banes of vampires are <i>also</i> things that would form the foundation of humanity's path as makers of tools and changers of the enviroment around them. For <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Control_of_fire_by_early_humans\" target=\"_blank\">a very vague and loose definition of humanity</a>, that is.<br /> <br /> I think there's a supernaturally-induced &quot;flashback&quot; of sorts in the Mekhet clanbook, one of a series of visions Frances Black has under the influence of the Glass Harmonium, relating to pre-historic humans or hominims even being stalked by a creature made of shadow, smoke, tentacles and spikes, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-17-2023, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T12:23:24-07:00","id":1518950,"title":"","content":"Was thinking again about some of the old games from my childhood and the weird homebrew rules we came up with for them.<br /> <br /> I mentioned earlier how we had custom rules for Mages that were crudely kitbashed with D&amp;D 3.5 as a guide of sorts. When you made a mortal, you could take a five-dot merit at character creation to be either a Mage or have True Faith. We knew about True Faith from Masquerade from my Dad, who played VTM back in the early 90's and told us about that aspect.<br /> <br /> In essence, both the Mage merit and the True Faith merit let you cast spells. The Mage merit let you use arcane magic and the True Faith merit let you cast divine magic. The Mage merit also gave you the &quot;Detect Magic&quot; spell automatically (and also let you determine if something or someone was supernatural) while True Faith let you use holy symbols and relics to deal aggravated damage to vampires and other undead as well as cast divine spells<br /> <br /> The spells were taken from D&amp;D but were arranged like Disciplines and you rolled Intelligence + Occult to cast the spells. Each school of magic or divine domain was set up like a discipline with five levels, each one a spell.<br /> <br /> I do remember that Magic Missile did two dots worth of lethal damage at range and Acid Arrow did the same but it was aggravated. <br /> <br /> Yeah, it was crude and broken but we were ignorant tweens who didn't have the money to just buy a copy of Mage The Awakening but still wanted mages in our games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T12:02:04-07:00","id":1519893,"title":"","content":"The Annunaki bloodline was quite interesting to read, but alas I couldn't think of a good idea for a player character let alone an npc for that matter along with the Invictus Houses which would really concentrate power to a select group of monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T13:57:18-07:00","id":1519897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>veiros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1518164#post1518164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I write with Google Translate)<br /> VtR has been released in Japanese (1e), but it is very minor.<br /> <br /> My first VtR character was a ghoul.<br /> My first VtR play was on a Japanese irc channel, 1 storyteller, 1 player.<br /> <br /> I was trying hard to decipher &quot;TheBlood&quot; and &quot;Ghouls&quot; with Google Translate.<br /> It was a pity that clanbook was difficult to translate with Google due to the layout <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1e and 2e both have their good points and both have their bad points.<br /> I thought about 1.7e, which incorporates the good points, but VtR has multiple rules intertwined, so it's quite difficult.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess i've gotten too used to just getting and using the books in english through the years.<br /> It has probably been a little too long since i last thought about how much of a headache and limited getting books in one's native language can be - or relying on Google Translate to guide you through reading original PDFs.<br /> <br /> Damn, i'm remembering a time when there was no Google Translate and it would be you all on your own with a few dictionaries to support if you were doing some english course on the side.<br /> <br /> Good luck either way, but do try to get yourself some english classes, wanting to translate RPG books is already a major incentive to help you and in the long run knowing another language will open a lot of doors to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T16:03:21-07:00","id":1519906,"title":"","content":"I always wanted to revisit these old-school games but the issue would be getting players who'd be willing to stick with 1e nWoD/Storytelling System rules and setting.<br /> <br /> I also kinda wanted to look back again at some of the 1e nWoD fangames again, maybe even come up with one of my own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T18:39:58-07:00","id":1519912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1519893#post1519893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Annunaki bloodline was quite interesting to read, but alas I couldn't think of a good idea for a player character let alone an npc for that matter along with the Invictus Houses which would really concentrate power to a select group of monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> It has been a number of years since i last read on the Annunaki, but must admit the bloodline always interested me far more for the sheer age implied in the backstory and questions left in the air by their presence in modern times than their actual ties and role in the Invictus.<br /> <br /> The two times i did use them was for a &quot;Lara Croft, Indiana Jones and the Colonial Marines meets Imhotep &amp; his Aliens&quot; game done adapting <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ruins_of_Ur\" target=\"_blank\">Ruins of Ur</a> and a &quot;Conan the Barbarian with vampires&quot; game mixing the bloodline's backstory from the Invictus book with elements from <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Belial&#39;s_Brood_(book)\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Akhud\" target=\"_blank\">Ahranite</a> mythologies, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Immortals\" target=\"_blank\">bloodbathers</a>, and the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ancient_Mysteries\" target=\"_blank\">Black Streets of Babylon</a> &quot;dark era&quot;. Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T20:03:36-07:00","id":1519921,"title":"","content":"This is more of a general nWoD 1e nostalgia thing and less of a Requiem thing, but I was thinking about the sheer amount of fangames that nWoD had.<br /> <br /> Of the two, <i>Genius: The Transgression</i> and <i>Princess: The Hopeful</i> are probably the most popular and both of them even got 2e CofD updates but I'll admit, I also had some interest in checking out the more obscure or forgotten nWoD 1e fan games like <i>Pathogen: The Infected</i> or the many nWoD attempts at giving all of the then-untouched oWoD games like Wraith, Mummy, and Demon back in the 2000's.<br /> <br /> Heck, even Genius and Princess began as more roundabout nWoD updates to oWoD stuff. Genius was a way to bring back all the sci-fi elements from <i>Mage: The Ascension</i> that didn't make it into Awakening and Princess was a more or less a serious attempt at making an nWoD equivalent of<i> Senshi: The Merchandising</i> (so it's pretty much a fan game of a fan game when you think about it that way)<br /> <br /> I've thought about doing something similar except the problem is that pretty much all the oWoD games got some form of nWoD reimaging (Wraith is kinda sorta the odd man out, but <i>Geist: The Sin-Eaters</i> is close enough in my book)<br /> <br /> With fan games, Senshi has Princess as it's nWoD equivalent and <i>Zombie: The Coil</i> could have Promethean, Beast, or Pathogen for its nWoD/CofD equivalent depending on how you look at it...<br /> <br /> But then there's <i>Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game</i>...<br /> <br /> Yeah, Street Fighter wasn't officially part of the classic WoD, but according to some of the old-timers I've talked to IRL, Street Fighter being mixed in with certain WoD chronicles wasn't that completely unheard of. And it did get a spiritual successor via WoD: Combat and IIRC, one of the Mirrors supplements included the combat card system from that adapted to nWoD.<br /> <br /> And I'm thinking, why not do a spiritual remake of that game with another beloved fighting game franchise that's a personal fave of mine? Something that used the 1e Storytelling System the same way SF used the oWoD Storyteller System.<br /> <br /> So, here's my basic proposal...<br /> <br /> <b>Dead Or Alive: The Storytelling Game</b><br /> <br /> And since this is an unofficial fan project, it could be easily worked into the toolkit mystery setting that was nWoD in the mid-2000's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T23:10:49-07:00","id":1519936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1519921#post1519921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then there's <i>Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game</i>...<br /> <br /> Yeah, Street Fighter wasn't officially part of the classic WoD, but according to some of the old-timers I've talked to IRL, Street Fighter being mixed in with certain WoD chronicles wasn't that completely unheard of. And it did get a spiritual successor via WoD: Combat and IIRC, one of the Mirrors supplements included the combat card system from that adapted to nWoD.<br /> <br /> And I'm thinking, why not do a spiritual remake of that game with another beloved fighting game franchise that's a personal fave of mine? Something that used the 1e Storytelling System the same way SF used the oWoD Storyteller System.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, i remember that one, STed and played a bunch of times, got all the books (even some who were kind of cash grabs like Perfect Warrior or Contenders). Also remember people kitbashing Ryu &amp; co into their WoD games, tweaking things by the use of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Combat\" target=\"_blank\">Combat</a> as a sort of bridge/roseta stone, sometimes straight porting things with quite ludricous lopsided results.<br /> <br /> From experience and the tales of the time, such &quot;crossovers&quot; seemed to be more of a one-time break for funsies than anything. The tones and themes are just too divergent overall.<br /> <br /> When it comes to a platform for a spiritual remake of <i>Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game</i>\u200b (or a bunch of settings taken from fighting games or beat 'em ups) i'd suggest you look into the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Trinity_Universe\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum</a> instead, that has a spirit far more focused into adventure, action and some degree of super-heroics cinematic milieu that Street Fighter and other franchises draw inspiration from.<br /> <br /> Words from one who has messed a lot with Storyteller-derived systems that did draw some mechanic influences from Street Fighter, like the original Aberrant or Exalted, for some examples.<br /> Damn, i still have notes of a Street Fighter chronicle that got interrupted by the pandemic among my files somewhere...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T08:20:51-07:00","id":1519954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1519936#post1519936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, i remember that one, STed and played a bunch of times, got all the books (even some who were kind of cash grabs like Perfect Warrior or Contenders). Also remember people kitbashing Ryu &amp; co into their WoD games, tweaking things by the use of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Combat\" target=\"_blank\">Combat</a> as a sort of bridge/roseta stone, sometimes straight porting things with quite ludricous lopsided results.<br /> <br /> From experience and the tales of the time, such &quot;crossovers&quot; seemed to be more of a one-time break for funsies than anything. The tones and themes are just too divergent overall.<br /> <br /> When it comes to a platform for a spiritual remake of <i>Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game</i>\u200b (or a bunch of settings taken from fighting games or beat 'em ups) i'd suggest you look into the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Trinity_Universe\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum</a> instead, that has a spirit far more focused into adventure, action and some degree of super-heroics cinematic milieu that Street Fighter and other franchises draw inspiration from.<br /> <br /> Words from one who has messed a lot with Storyteller-derived systems that did draw some mechanic influences from Street Fighter, like the original Aberrant or Exalted, for some examples.<br /> Damn, i still have notes of a Street Fighter chronicle that got interrupted by the pandemic among my files somewhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>Trinity never caught my interest before but I'll look into it.<br /> <br /> When it came to &quot;the themes&quot; of WoD/CofD, I was always a maverick so I've got no issue having fighting game characters interact with vampires and werewolves and the like,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T13:59:56-07:00","id":1520149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1519906#post1519906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always wanted to revisit these old-school games but the issue would be getting players who'd be willing to stick with 1e nWoD/Storytelling System rules and setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read most of the VtR 1ed stuff but never played it. Trying to talk my friends into trying it again, or 2ed even but they are focused on V5 these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T15:22:54-07:00","id":1522433,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the thread necromancy but I just uncovered an old memory of mine after talking with my brothers on the phone.<br /> <br /> We had a whole system of ghouled animals that were called &quot;chimera&quot;, with the Hellhounds from the Requiem 1e corebook simply being the most common type of chimera. There were other chimera who had different names based on mythical creatures.<br /> <br /> And then I began thinking and I came up with some concept ideas for this &quot;hierarchy&quot; of ghouled animals.<br /> <br /> Most chimerae/ghoul animals are rare, with the exceptions of the hellhound, the hellcat, and the griffon.<br /> <br /> <b>Hellhound</b>: Dogs, Wolves, Coyotes, Jackals<br /> <br /> <b>Hellcat: </b>Cats, Lynxes, Lions, Bobcats, Tigers, Leopards, Panthers<br /> <br /> <b>Griffon: </b>Flying birds and bats. Ravens, crows, vultures, hawks, pigeons, and vampire bats are the most common animals to be turned into griffons.<br /> <br /> <b>Basilisk: </b>Reptiles and flightless birds. Snakes, monitor lizards, and alligators are the most common animals to become basilisks. A ghouled flightless bird (such as a chicken or an ostrich) is sometimes called a <b>Cockatrice</b> instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Arion: </b>Horses, mules, and donkeys. Arions were once as common as hellhounds, hellcats, and griffons are today, but the advent of automobiles, motorcycles, and trains have rendered them largely a relic cherished by a few elder vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Warpig: </b>Pigs, Boars, Javelinas, Peccaries, Warthogs. Often used as either attack animals or as a way to indirectly ghoul people by feeding them pork taken from warpigs.<br /> <br /> <b>Minotaur: </b>Cattle, Bison, Oxen, and Buffalo. Used as attack animals, beasts of burden, or &quot;proxy ghouling&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Triton: </b>Fish, amphibians, eels, dolphins, crustaceans, shellfish. Tritons are almost exclusively kept either for proxy ghouling or in private menageries of elder vampires. Though it is rumored that some elders in coastal areas would give their blood to sharks, barracudas, lampreys, or pikes to create attack tritons<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, another thing in our Requiem games was &quot;proxy ghouling&quot;. If a human ate meat from ghouled animals or vegetables and fruits from ghouled plants enough times, they'd eventually become a ghoul. It was a lot slower and more inefficient than giving blood directly, but also a lot stealthier and subtler and was more common in the pre-industrial era.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why so many Kindred even in the modern nights will still create mandragora and chimeras, and usually sell them to unwitting kine via food trucks and farmer's markets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 09-11-2023, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T23:09:04-07:00","id":1523990,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the thread necromancy but does anyone else have any good 1e nostalgia? <br /> <br /> In particular, I'm curious if anyone got their start in early nWoD 1e without having already started with one of the Classic WoD games....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T00:52:18-07:00","id":1523993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1523990#post1523990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for the thread necromancy but does anyone else have any good 1e nostalgia?<br /> <br /> In particular, I'm curious if anyone got their start in early nWoD 1e without having already started with one of the Classic WoD games....</div> </div> </div> </div>I started with 3rd ed. Dark Age and Masquerade, then moved to 1st ed. Requiem and now I've been playing 2nd Ed. since so many years. I honestly do not feel any nostalgia of 1st ed requiem which I thought it had some badly designed feature (mechanics and lore) that I think got fixed with 2nd edition - at least for what concerns my personal tastes - keeping intact the mood, and what was good from the 1st ed. <br /> Don't take me wrong, 2nd edition is far to be perfect and something would need to be reworked or updated, but all included I like 2nd ed the most at the moment. I also tried to go for Masquerade v5 but I really dislike it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T10:58:35-07:00","id":1524066,"title":"","content":"I got involved on the tail end of Vampire The Masquerade when they started to wind down the line and not long afterwards saw the 1st edition of VTR and found myself interested in it despite the blurred reflections flaw and initally having only pale echoes of emotions. I'm glad that they did away with emotional issue but I'm still so so on the blurred reflection flaw as everyone and there friend has a cellphone and record everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T11:04:32-07:00","id":1524068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1524066#post1524066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got involved on the tail end of Vampire The Masquerade when they started to wind down the line and not long afterwards saw the 1st edition of VTR and found myself interested in it despite the blurred reflections flaw and initally having only pale echoes of emotions. I'm glad that they did away with emotional issue but I'm still so so on the blurred reflection flaw as everyone and there friend has a cellphone and record everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we always just ignored the &quot;pale shadows of emotions&quot; at our table and went back and forth on the blurred reflections.<br /> <br /> During the crazy games I played and ran as a kid back in the mid-2000's, smartphones weren't a thing and cell phone cameras were all kinda shit and not every fliphone had them so we kinda rolled with blurred reflections. The way we did it was that regular mirrors weren't really affected by a vampire and neither did still photograph cameras but video cameras of any kind brought out the blurred reflections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T19:30:12-07:00","id":1524080,"title":"","content":"I miss virtue and vice, honestly, I do like the 2.e got rid of the whole imitation of emotions, old humanity system, and fog of ages. These changes all made vampires more human so the mask and dirge aspect that made vampires only pretend humans with their masks kind of seems like a sidestep away from that. It also does not really play well in a mortals game where the players are turned into vampires since humans still use virtue and vice.<br /> <br /> I just never really liked the concept of masks and who you are in the dark because realistically everyone wears many masks not just one who you are among friends may be different than who you are among coworkers, or strangers for some examples. But a virtue is something you always have; it is a concept you idolize and attempt to emulate among all people whereas a vice is a negative trait that is also always a part of you. <br /> <br /> I just feel they represent vastly different things. Those things in the sense of virtue and vice are also things I prefer. They made an excellent system for it in the chronicles core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T04:16:36-07:00","id":1524091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1524080#post1524080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I miss virtue and vice, honestly, I do like the 2.e got rid of the whole imitation of emotions, old humanity system, and fog of ages. These changes all made vampires more human so the mask and dirge aspect that made vampires only pretend humans with their masks kind of seems like a sidestep away from that. It also does not really play well in a mortals game where the players are turned into vampires since humans still use virtue and vice.<br /> <br /> I just never really liked the concept of masks and who you are in the dark because realistically everyone wears many masks not just one who you are among friends may be different than who you are among coworkers, or strangers for some examples. But a virtue is something you always have; it is a concept you idolize and attempt to emulate among all people whereas a vice is a negative trait that is also always a part of you.<br /> <br /> I just feel they represent vastly different things. Those things in the sense of virtue and vice are also things I prefer. They made an excellent system for it in the chronicles core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree that Mask ane Dirge are one of the biggest flaws of 2ed. I'm still trying to use those but it's clear how my players are in difficulty to really stick to or interpret it. And some mask/dirge is quite unbalanced compared to others, with the result that PCs are sometime forcing themeselves to make something according to the dirge/Mask just to regain some WP. Which I don't feel it's how it should be. So I would probably rather get back to Vice and virtue system as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T09:00:48-07:00","id":1524101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1524068#post1524068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, we always just ignored the &quot;pale shadows of emotions&quot; at our table and went back and forth on the blurred reflections.<br /> <br /> During the crazy games I played and ran as a kid back in the mid-2000's, smartphones weren't a thing and cell phone cameras were all kinda shit and not every fliphone had them so we kinda rolled with blurred reflections. The way we did it was that regular mirrors weren't really affected by a vampire and neither did still photograph cameras but video cameras of any kind brought out the blurred reflections.</div> </div> </div> </div>You ever have one of those Razor phones? They were all the rage when I was in school lol.<br /> <br /> I kind of had a similar rule I argued that the beast or rather the vampire subconsciously knows when it is more useful to be blurred or not show in a mirror, so if you are in for example a funhouse filled with mirrors and other people are there you would show up, to me it is the only way that the masquerade can be maintained as cameras / mirrors are everywhere. <br /> <br /> Another more classic angle that I have used is that vampires only cast no reflection under silver backed mirrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T09:17:38-07:00","id":1524102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1524091#post1524091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do agree that Mask ane Dirge are one of the biggest flaws of 2ed. I'm still trying to use those but it's clear how my players are in difficulty to really stick to or interpret it. And some mask/dirge is quite unbalanced compared to others, with the result that PCs are sometime forcing themeselves to make something according to the dirge/Mask just to regain some WP. Which I don't feel it's how it should be. So I would probably rather get back to Vice and virtue system as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been toying with removing it, so I took Mr Gones, 10 dot requiem 2.e character sheet and used a pdf editor to put in virtue and vice instead of mask and dirge. Only gameplay change I think I would have to make is giving a more extreme reward for virtue and vice like mask and dirge had.<br /> <br /> Say for instance you had virtue loyal, to gain 1 willpower you would have to stand up for your group to your own detriment or minor risk, however you could refresh all your willpower if you let your loyalty put you in extreme personal danger such as taking a severe blow for an ally or suffering a breaking point to defend your allies.<br /> <br /> If you had the vice spiteful, you would gain 1 willpower by getting back at someone who had rightly wronged you, this would have to be petty or cruel to gain thepoint. You would gain all willpower if you &quot;cut off your nose to spite your face&quot; i.e as a result of your spite you ended up just as bad off as the one you went against and were happy with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","user":"BloodyRelight","date":". 10-15-2023, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T10:50:04-07:00","id":1524109,"title":"","content":"There is nothing to stop us from using elements from the first edition and I do like Virtue and Vice and would still use it our vtr games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T12:50:52-07:00","id":1524114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1524109#post1524109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing to stop us from using elements from the first edition and I do like Virtue and Vice and would still use it our vtr games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I overal like much more 2ed system (discipline design at first) but using some old feature from 1ed is not game breaker at all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T04:08:36-07:00","id":1524135,"title":"","content":"Sorry for veering away a little bit Matt, another thing I miss was the huge amounts of unique disciplines 1.e had, I know none more dark publishing has been making 2.e versions of the bloodline books but these books have removed several of the disciplines and replaced them with devotions. <br /> <br /> 1.e Had some crazy Ideas for bloodlines and their disciplines. My favorite was the Amara Havana from ancient bloodlines their bloodline curse was so cool, they would leave behind illusory bloody hand prints on objects they touched. They had a really interesting discipline that was kind of like protean and blood sorcery fused together, they did get a ridiculously broken ability at the fourth dot that let them treat rain as blood though, which made their elders very powerful especially if they mastered creation through cruac or theban sorcery so I understand why they were changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T11:07:02-08:00","id":1525212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1524135#post1524135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for veering away a little bit Matt, another thing I miss was the huge amounts of unique disciplines 1.e had, I know none more dark publishing has been making 2.e versions of the bloodline books but these books have removed several of the disciplines and replaced them with devotions.<br /> <br /> 1.e Had some crazy Ideas for bloodlines and their disciplines. My favorite was the Amara Havana from ancient bloodlines their bloodline curse was so cool, they would leave behind illusory bloody hand prints on objects they touched. They had a really interesting discipline that was kind of like protean and blood sorcery fused together, they did get a ridiculously broken ability at the fourth dot that let them treat rain as blood though, which made their elders very powerful especially if they mastered creation through cruac or theban sorcery so I understand why they were changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never got to delve too deep into all the bloodlines 1e had, but I really want to and with the way the Requiem 1e game I'm running with my hubby is going, I might look into buying some of the Bloodlines books","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T21:33:38-08:00","id":1525421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1525212#post1525212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never got to delve too deep into all the bloodlines 1e had, but I really want to and with the way the Requiem 1e game I'm running with my hubby is going, I might look into buying some of the Bloodlines books</div> </div> </div> </div>I would really recommend it some of them add a lot of flavor! If you want an overview of the bloodline disciplines you can check the codex of darkness this section has an overview of the clan specific disciplines and the books they are found in. It was very helpful for me since it helped me rule out books I did not want. <a href=\"https://codexofdarkness.com/wiki/Disciplines,_Bloodline_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Disciplines, Bloodline (1st Edition) - Codex of Darkness</a>\u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-14T15:21:25-08:00","id":1525435,"title":"","content":"I personally go with the Gangrel bloodlines myself if I was ever decided to use them myself or some of the Invictus lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T11:28:30-07:00","id":1533521,"title":"","content":"We're getting close to the 20th Anniversary of Requiem 1e in August","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T12:15:17-07:00","id":1533524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1533521#post1533521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're getting close to the 20th Anniversary of Requiem 1e in August</div> </div> </div> </div>Feels like it was just yesterday that I was making my first Nosferatu elder dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T13:40:32-07:00","id":1533533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1523990#post1523990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for the thread necromancy but does anyone else have any good 1e nostalgia?<br /> <br /> In particular, I'm curious if anyone got their start in early nWoD 1e without having already started with one of the Classic WoD games....</div> </div> </div> </div>I did\u2014I was first introduced to<i> Changeling: the Lost</i> and then the first edition of <i>Requiem</i>, long before I discovered either of the two's predecessors in the cWoD. I tend to prefer <i>Masquerade</i> to <i>Requiem</i> nowadays, but the first edition of <i>Requiem</i> continues to be a source of nostalgia (&amp; inspiration for my own writing endeavours)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T14:24:53-07:00","id":1535040,"title":"","content":"Myself I came in at the tail end of the Vampire The Masquerade series and found that I really enjoyed VTR 1st edition despite it's flaws and I still like both settings along with Changeling The Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T20:18:20-07:00","id":1535245,"title":"","content":"I finally broke down and got Requiem in '08. Instead of going out to the bars like I normally did on a Saturday, I stayed in and read Requiem, the whole night. It was like every question anyone had that played V:tM, was answered in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T13:00:00-07:00","id":1535298,"title":"","content":"Congrats on getting the answers to whatever question you had Iguazu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T18:23:14-07:00","id":1535312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1535298#post1535298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congrats on getting the answers to whatever question you had Iguazu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, what happens if I get into a town and I can't find the Prince; in V:tM, I was really, really worried about that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T20:05:42-07:00","id":1537931,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I honestly would love to see more love for Requiem 1e, especially since the 20th anniversary of it (and the rest of Chronicles) is only a month and a half away now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T20:11:22-07:00","id":1537932,"title":"","content":"I like both Masquerade and Requiem for different reasons, though I\u2019m only familiar with Requiem 2e. They\u2019re like parallel worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T22:29:30-07:00","id":1537933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1537932#post1537932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like both Masquerade and Requiem for different reasons, though I\u2019m only familiar with Requiem 2e. They\u2019re like parallel worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do too (well, except V5. I hate that one)<br /> <br /> I'm more familiar with Requiem 1e and prefer it to 2e, but I respect 2e and its efforts to distinguish its parallel world more from Masquerade's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T01:36:44-07:00","id":1537934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1537933#post1537933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do too (well, except V5. I hate that one)<br /> <br /> I'm more familiar with Requiem 1e and prefer it to 2e, but I respect 2e and its efforts to distinguish its parallel world more from Masquerade's.</div> </div> </div> </div>While i do agree V5 has issues with formatting/editing, mechanics and setting (dis)continuity, i don't quite hate it. It <b>has </b>generated a lot of discussion on setting, metaplot &amp; lore, something that i find engaging and useful. To paraphrase something i read from an interview by Tarantino &quot;it's simpler to adapt a trainwreck into something worthwhile than adapting in a worthwhile way what's already a classic&quot; - it has issues on several levels imho, but those help throw light in a number of lore or metaplot elements we can be sometimes too quick to accept acritically.<br /> <br /> Do i play it? Hell, no. Zero desire to reinvent the wheel when i wanted to get people playing as soon as possible - for that V20 as base platform that i tweak, mangle &amp; houserule to taste has been pretty much wonderful.<br /> <br /> And yet i have kind of adopted Loresheets (most of them homebrew) for the chronicle, mixed some NPCs from Chicago by Night 5e (from 1e Chicago too, long story) &amp; Let the Streets Run Red in my version of Milwaukee, had an attack on the Vienna chantry (by completely different parts, different results and aftereffects) and have been thinking of giving Fall of London something of a (massive) retool, for when i take the chronicle out of its current hiatus (work issues <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).\u200b<br /> <br /> To be clear - while i've been in a &quot;Masquerade nostalgia&quot; mode for the last year or so, i still love Requiem to bits and know for sure will eventually return to playing or STing on it when the mood to <i>really </i>make my own thing and brand of setting/worldbuilding hits me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T13:06:35-07:00","id":1538950,"title":"","content":"The Covenants were a great idea for Vampire The Reqiuem and having much fewer clans that didn't step on each other toes for what theme they represented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T04:41:42-07:00","id":1540268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread#post1517651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, let's get the elephant in the room out of the way. Me and my friends never did personal horror. Back then, we always found that aspect kind of lame and boring. To us, it felt like they were trying to make the game seem more artsy than it was and as we came from D&amp;D 3.5 and were into stuff like anime, action movies, and vidya, we went full &quot;Supers with fangs&quot; as some of the fandom may derisively call it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ain't nothing wrong with &quot;Supers with fangs&quot; and it doesn't have to be incompatible with personal horror.<br /> <br /> Live a double life. Juggle two, mostly non-overlapping, extensive groups of friends, and yet always be terribly alone. Be bothered about all the lies, but not about to stop. Strike from the shadows or own the room, or switch back and forth. Never have enough time in the night to do it all. Occasionally need a moment to weep on a rooftop.<br /> <br /> Who's that? Batman. Or a perfectly viable vampire character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T08:11:30-07:00","id":1540841,"title":"","content":"So, today is the 20th Anniversary","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T10:54:43-07:00","id":1540900,"title":"","content":"Where does the time go? It seems like it was only yesterday that we had people sad about the ending of the old World of Darkness line and the uncertainty of the new line and how people would react to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T19:50:08-07:00","id":1541561,"title":"","content":"I do remember eagerly awaiting for Ordo Dracul to come out and learn more about their covenant and what Dracula might be up to and why the clans would be attracted to the Ordo Dracul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T17:57:56-07:00","id":1543128,"title":"","content":"I remember reading that Requiem got greenlit for a movie from New Line Cinema back in 2004 when the game came out, but nothing ever really came of it.<br /> <br /> I wonder if there's a story behind that or if that was an open-and-shut case of the studio buying the film rights just in case and then forgetting they even had it after a certain point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T01:00:52-07:00","id":1543140,"title":"","content":"I heard the same story myself Matt, but I didn't put much stock in it as stuff like this seems quite common and I put it down as rumors and I seem to recall around the same time there was talk about a movie treatment for Palladium Books Rifts series or at least a game happening and I don't recall anything happening there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T11:40:23-07:00","id":1543154,"title":"","content":"IP is optioned for movies much more frequently than plans actually materialize to use those options, I believe.","signatur