 shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T11:58:01-07:00","id":1543897,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's a bad show that lasted longer then it should and characters having powers they shouldn't have or not freaking out when they were near candle lit room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-15-2024, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T20:27:07-07:00","id":1544339,"title":"","content":"So, I was reading Damnation-City, and they cite Se7en as a movie-inspiration to watch and so, I looked up film-locations; it was filmed in Los Angeles, and I remembered my idea for a city; the City of Angels, based off of LA, and create a map with seven-hills (virtues); I've started on several-versions, but haven't completed any. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1543897#post1543897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that's a bad show that lasted longer then it should and characters having powers they shouldn't have or not freaking out when they were near candle lit room.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had difficulty watching it because of its lameness, but I have to have some integrity and say, like I say about <i>Rings of Power</i>; I'm just glad they did something with the IP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T17:37:35-07:00","id":1552248,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the thread necromancy but I've been waxing nostalgic again while reading the Requiem corebook and I wonder how many here would ever be interested in a Requiem 1e game as a play-by-post? I know Requiem 2e is way more popular (and understandably so) but I'm not gonna lie, I have a major soft spot for VTR 1e and prefer it over 2e.<br /> <br /> Like, I unironically like the &quot;Masquerade Lite&quot; approach that early Requiem 1e had a lot. Yeah, it's mainly due to nostalgia but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T09:38:22-07:00","id":1552262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1552248#post1552248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the thread necromancy but I've been waxing nostalgic again while reading the Requiem corebook and I wonder how many here would ever be interested in a Requiem 1e game as a play-by-post? I know Requiem 2e is way more popular (and understandably so) but I'm not gonna lie, I have a major soft spot for VTR 1e and prefer it over 2e.<br /> <br /> Like, I unironically like the &quot;Masquerade Lite&quot; approach that early Requiem 1e had a lot. Yeah, it's mainly due to nostalgia but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less than a whole year of inactivity, so not really necromancy, just mild ressurectionist work.<br /> And i can relate, a bunch of years later, still too lazy to fully dive into CotD and Requiem 2e mechanics.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for players, you can count me in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-12-2025, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T00:25:02-08:00","id":1555305,"title":"","content":"The one time I ran Requiem, it was 1e. I had all the books available at the time and all my players were down for Ordo Dracul, so they essentially became the entire local branch of the OD for the city and we had a blast. ran that game for a couple of years and after awhile it got kinda funny.<br /> They were deciding which Coils to pursue based on what their overall Ordo Dracul title would evolve to depending on what they had at what level and strangely, all of them started taking various hand to hand fighting merits due to trouble in town. Mostly because you can take someone's sword or gun, but not their skills, there was also the idea that improving themselves by relying on skill and Disciplines to defend themselves was more authentically Ordo Dracul in philosophy than just getting strapped would be.<br /> By the time the game reached it's final few months, the whole coterie were secret society occultist vampire kung fu masters, essentially, and the local branch, which consisted of them, a few progeny, and a few recruits they'd taken on board over the course of the game as the couple of remaining vampires on hand who'd recruited them had either moved on, died, or gone into torpor were <i><b>all </b></i>secret society occultist vampire martial artists because they'd assimilated the idea that punching face was an essential part of the Ordo Dracul Way.<br /> It was also pointed out that martial artists meditating on spiritually potent land to enhance their powers was basically one of the essential tropes of the Xianxia genre of Chinese novels, which means that the Ordo Dracul could be considered a vampire cultivation sect.<br /> It was a lot of fun, even had some crossover stuff a few times as they beefed with mages and werewolves over who got to use Dragon Nests for their various cultural purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28938-madgreenson","name":"MadGreenSon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28938_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-01T16:36:36-08:00","id":1557193,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a blast and a good example of how local covenants might differ from the stereotype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T10:31:05-08:00","id":1557345,"title":"","content":"With just the <i>amazing </i>nWoD core, and Requiem 1E, and the Antagonists book, I remember running a very fun one-shot along the lines of <i>Night of the Living Dead </i>meets World of Darkness. One character was a vampire, another was a mortal, and I think another had Supernatural Merits from the core. This was before any of the other books had come out, mind you. We had a lot of fun seeing what happened as a vampire tried to survive a zombie outbreak and also preserve his only food source (can't drink from zombies, yick!). <br /> <br /> That poor vampire was out of his depth. Between the zombies, and the ghosts that followed in their wake, it was a difficult situation. Lots of fun, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T18:10:06-08:00","id":1557358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1557345#post1557345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With just the <i>amazing </i>nWoD core, and Requiem 1E, and the Antagonists book, I remember running a very fun one-shot along the lines of <i>Night of the Living Dead </i>meets World of Darkness. One character was a vampire, another was a mortal, and I think another had Supernatural Merits from the core. This was before any of the other books had come out, mind you. We had a lot of fun seeing what happened as a vampire tried to survive a zombie outbreak and also preserve his only food source (can't drink from zombies, yick!).<br /> <br /> That poor vampire was out of his depth. Between the zombies, and the ghosts that followed in their wake, it was a difficult situation. Lots of fun, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>A game some friends ran end up having a bit of that too through a Morbus blood cult messing around with &quot;unlocking the (zombie) apocalypse&quot; blending the use of Cachexy with blood magic and mass Larva (from Wicked Dead) creation. Things were eventually contained by the kindred status quo, but not without massive stretching of the Masquerade by borderline Buffy end season events and the extensive media, Dominate &amp; Majesty abuse to put a clampdown on things.<br /> <br /> (Still resulted in a lot of headaches as the kindred would bump into hundred if not thousands of hunters or other people more aware and willing to adress the matter of the supernatural than the new undead court would prefer who slipped through the cracks of their attempts to bring things to a semblance of the previous status quo of normalcy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T19:18:13-08:00","id":1557359,"title":"","content":"That sounds like an amazing game! For the players. The characters? Not so much....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T22:57:15-08:00","id":1557364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1557359#post1557359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like an amazing game! For the players. The characters? Not so much....</div> </div> </div> </div>Things were quite wild for all parts involved, even though all of the characters involved were already ancillae-elders with quite decent experience and influence. In fact some of the spectacular mess took form because of their own maneuverings to set up the field for the return of a previous prince to the throne ended crisscrossing with older layers of intrigue they were not wholy aware of (only one of the five PCs was in the city in the turn of the 20th century, when &quot;the Morbus cult&quot; had been eliminated by a multi-covenant front formed by the prince of the time, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T18:39:34-07:00","id":1559261,"title":"","content":"I've always considered (a conspiracy-theory), as soon as Requiem came out, that, Vampire the Masquerade was based off of real life accounts from real vampires and turned into a game; Requiem, however, is how REAL vampires are!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T20:37:06-07:00","id":1559263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadGreenSon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517651-1e-vampire-the-requiem-nostalgia-thread?p=1555305#post1555305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one time I ran Requiem, it was 1e. I had all the books available at the time and all my players were down for Ordo Dracul, so they essentially became the entire local branch of the OD for the city and we had a blast. ran that game for a couple of years and after awhile it got kinda funny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they did.<br /> <br /> <b>ST:</b> <i>&quot;Alright, so your choice of covenants are the (not) Camarilla, the (not) Anarchs, the-&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Players:</b> <i>&quot;We wanna be Dracula!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>ST:</b> <i>&quot;Ordo Dracul, it is!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}